PATCH 633: restore the original early resource vectors and boot222f call operands.

Original CRT 223c executes XOR BX,BX / MOV SI,0174 / CALL SS:[12]. BX zero
resolves the relocation table through SS:[74]; it does not make F842 inert.
The actual paired original records all140 fetches and16 far-vector writes,
including resource-open388=2082:306c. Reuse fist_apply_reloc_section for the
rebased table, which emits the corresponding0f69 segment and original offsets.
Patch091's early-install corruption claim was caused by later dropped operands.

Original boot222f sets BX=6b78, CX=DS and DX=6b7e and inherits BP from the
actual1345 memory-list lookup. Publish that existing owner through the callee's
four-argument type. Do not seed1718 or zero-pad unknown lanes. Patch632 already
fixes the reached three-miss callee; the source-proven loaded-bit skip remains.

Remove the delayed098 vector installation and133 MSPRITE0 retry from e714.
The original e714 starts with BE0E(4); common sprites are loaded by the actual
cae6/153c startup call. The shared harness marks scripted-input availability at
the same e714 presentation boundary without reinstalling resource state.

Evidence: engine-resource-registers/source-proof.json (original CRT/registers),
engine-font-loader/source-proof.json (three actual BACKLAND misses),
engine-live-bp/source-proof.json and engine-resource-skip/source-proof.json.
The reaching regression executes the emitted CRT/caller and real DOS dispatcher,
checking all16 vector writes and whole16MiB outputs; parent Native/WASM fail.
Legacy pre-install INT/ES writes are retained in a before snapshot, not hidden.
CPU flags/guest stack/instruction timing and the dynamic153c fullEBX return,
final mixed PCM and first original frame817 remain separate open contracts.
